A `cast` is a map on each `point` Waypoint naming the shape its sentences take, never content, each key true or absent, from a closed set: `terse` -- one short statement given at once, taking no elaboration after it, `plain` -- laid down without support, ground or qualification, `hedged` -- offered as a guess or forecast rather than asserted, `chained` -- a run of parallel items or alternatives inside one sentence, `asked` -- put as a question that takes no lead-in, `voiced` -- spoken in a named voice, the first person, an invitation, or words reported as another's, `instanced` -- one recognisable instance named and left without comment, `dated` -- each instance placed in time, or `figured` -- asserted as a likeness or a figurative identification.
